  "note": "Full unchanged measured-source files, two isolated production analysis workers with the same pool policy and calculation parameters. Baseline is an immutable archived production build from immediately before these core changes; optimized is the current production build. Only nearest-k scratch/coordinate buffers, invariant M3C2 cylinder geometry and SCS neighbourhood scratch differ in the candidate core. Both reuse exact M3C2 trees and Map quality nearest preparation after excluded setup. Each method gets fresh worker contexts and full inputs; five excluded alternating warm-up pairs precede ten timed pairs unless repeats overridden. Wall times include complete computation and RPC; SOR includes output indexing and ICP includes source transformation. ICP reloads an unchanged measured moving cloud before each call, with loading excluded, then fits point-to-plane for at most ten iterations at 0.8 overlap. Normal/SOR k=24, M3C2 normal/projection/depth/core spacing=0.4/0.25/0.5/0.25 m; map voxel/minimum occupancy/inlier threshold=1 m/5/0.5 m, scalar moments. Every pair checks all normal/M3C2/display distance bits, ICP transform/RMS/iterations/convergence, exact inlier metrics/statistics and byte-identical PLY for M3C2/SOR/ICP. Map AWD/SCS retain the existing 1e-12 relative/absolute HashMap reduction tolerance. Validation/exports/cleanup and loading/pool startup/setup are outside timing; no other builds/tests/scans run concurrently. Source/manifest/both-build/script hashes are checked before/after. Two contexts retain independent trees/heaps; each existing copy budget applies separately and is not a total process-memory cap. CPU clocks, power, GC and other applications are uncontrolled. Even/odd measured-source splits are not independent surveys or accuracy/registration ground truth. No GPU adapter or model information is collected."
